        "topic_names": [
          "4.2 VERSATILE NATURE OF CARBON"
        ],
        "answer": "The two main characteristics are (i) Catenation: Carbon has the unique ability to form bonds with other carbon atoms, creating long chains, branches, or rings. These bonds are strong and stable. (ii) Tetravalency: Carbon has a valency of four, allowing it to bond with four other carbon atoms or atoms of mono-valent elements like hydrogen, oxygen, nitrogen, sulphur, or halogens. Together, these properties, along with the formation of strong covalent bonds due to carbon's small size, enable the existence of millions of diverse carbon compounds.",
