          "4.2 VERSATILE NATURE OF CARBON"
        ],
        "answer": "Naming carbon compounds follows these steps: (i) Identify the number of carbon atoms. (ii) If a functional group is present, add the appropriate prefix or suffix. (iii) If a suffix starts with a vowel, drop the 'e' from the alkane name (e.g., Propane becomes propanone for a ketone). (iv) For unsaturated compounds, replace 'ane' with 'ene' or 'yne'. Examples: A three-carbon chain is propane. Adding a hydroxyl group creates propanol. A double-bonded three-carbon chain is propene, while a triple-bonded one is propyne.",
